be merged ([#4411](https://github.com/evanw/esbuild/issues/4411))"," ","     It's possible to configure esbuild such that separate output files end up with the same output path. For example, you could name all code splitting chunks `chunk` via the `chunkNames` setting, which might generate multiple output files with the same path `chunk.js`. This does not happen by default since by default the chunk names include a hash to make sure they're unique (e.g. named something like `chunk-GX7G2SBE.js` instead)."],"additions":4,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"Makefile","lines":["@@ -24,7 +24,7 @@ test-common: test-go vet-go no-filepath verify-source-map end-to-end-tests js-ap"," "," # These tests are for release (the extra tests are not included in \"test\" because they are pretty slow)"," test-all:","-\t@$(MAKE) --no-print-directory -j6 test-common test-deno ts-type-tests test-wasm-node test-wasm-browser lib-typecheck test-yarnpnp","+\t@$(MAKE) --no-print-directory -j6 test-common ts-type-tests test-wasm-node test-wasm-browser lib-typecheck test-yarnpnp"," "," check-go-version:"," \t@go version | grep -F \" go$(GO_VERSION) \" || (echo 'Please install Go version $(GO_VERSION)' && false)","@@ -98,16 +98,6 @@ test-wasm-node: esbuild"," test-wasm-browser: platform-wasm | scripts/browser/node_modules"," \tcd scripts/browser && node browser-tests.js"," ","-test-deno: esbuild platform-deno","-\tESBUILD_BINARY_PATH=\"$(shell pwd)/esbuild\" deno test --allow-run --allow-env --allow-net --allow-read --allow-write --no-check scripts/deno-tests.js","-\t@echo '✅ deno tests passed' # I couldn't find a Deno API for telling when tests have failed, so I'm doing this here instead","-\tESBUILD_BINARY_PATH=\"$(shell pwd)/esbuild\" deno eval 'import { transform, stop } from \"file://$(shell pwd)/deno/mod.js\"; console.log((await transform(\"1+2\")).code); stop()' | grep \"1 + 2;\"","-\tESBUILD_BINARY_PATH=\"$(shell pwd)/esbuild\" deno eval 'import { transform, stop } from \"file://$(s